<title>CHINA: China's top insurance firms spins off life unit.</title>
<headline>China's top insurance firms spins off life unit.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Shanghai branch of China's biggest insurance company, People's Insurance Company of China (PICC), has spun off its life insurance department as a separate firm, a company official said on Friday.</p>
<p>The official said the new firm, the People's Insurance (Life) Company of China Shanghai branch, would concentrate exclusively on selling life insurance policies, a market now dominated by U.S. firm American International Group.</p>
<p>He said PICC currently had about 40 percent of the fast-growing Shanghai life insurance market.</p>
</text>
